  "notes": [
    "Only J161055.6-112009 (J1610) retains an unbound/HVS candidacy in the final assessment. J154401.1-162451 (J1544) is excluded: the Figure 4 caption (T:p6-b0) mentions it above the illustrative solar-circle HVS limit, but the text applies the position-dependent criterion and reports its V_GRF as 523 ± 40 km/s, just below the expected escape speed of 570 km/s at its position (T:p10-b7), and the conclusion describes it as 'near but not above' escape speed (T:p12-b5). No individually identified star is studied as a previously known unbound candidate for follow-up.",
    "J161055.6-112009: Table 3 reports the right-ascension proper-motion component as mu_alpha cos(delta); it is recorded as proper_motion_ra without conversion (T:p12-b0, I:p12-b0). The target J1610 has V_GRF = 807 +/- 159 km/s in Table 4 (T:p12-b1) and 807 +/- 154 km/s in the Sec 3.4 text (T:p9-b7); both reported forms are retained. No per-star parallax or bound/unbound probability is reported."
  ]
